mfd/input: TSC2301 core, touchscreen and keypad; N800 DT node

The Nokia N800 has a TI TSC2301 on McSPI1 CS0: touchscreen, a 4x4
keypad (its d-pad and hardware keys) and the audio codec. Mainline never
had a driver for it (Nokia's lived only in the linux-omap and Maemo
trees), and the N800 DT had no node.

Ported from Nokia's 2.6.21 drivers (tsc2301-core.c, tsc2301_ts.c,
tsc2301_kp.c; GPL, Copyright (C) 2005-2007 Nokia Corporation, Juha
Yrjölä, Jarkko Oikarinen, Imre Deak):

- MFD core (CONFIG_MFD_TSC2301, "ti,tsc2301"): regmap over 16-bit SPI
  words (command = read bit 15 | page << 11 | address << 5, as Nokia
  sent them; CPU-endian buffers), the reset line pulsed as Nokia did,
  soft reset (0xbb00), the ADC/DAC reset values as ID check, keypad
  scanning stopped, the CONFIG2 shadow (bit 15 doesn't read back).
  The touchscreen and keypad are child devices sharing the chip's DT
  node. The keypad scan is restarted whenever the touchscreen scanning
  changes (Nokia's workaround for a scanner that gets stuck busy).
  The audio codec is not supported yet.
- Touchscreen (CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN_TSC2301): the errata's three-step ADC
  setup (8-sample averaging, 1 ms settling: Nokia's LS041Y3 settings),
  X/Y/Z1/Z2 read in one burst on DAV (falling edge, threaded), Nokia's
  filter (touch resistance limits 400 for the first sample and the
  max-pressure after, positions averaged over 4 samples, lowest
  resistance of the last 16, 8-unit dead zone), pen up after 20 ms
  without DAV. Scanning runs only while the input device is open (so
  "inhibited" replaces Nokia's disable_ts). Standard touchscreen-*
  properties and ti,x-plate-ohms.
- Keypad (CONFIG_KEYBOARD_TSC2301): "linux,keymap" with bit = row * 4 +
  column, unmapped keys masked in KPMASK, KBIRQ (falling edge) in
  interrupt mode 2 (released by reading KPDATA; Nokia: mode 0 can stick),
  Nokia's ghost-key filter, all keys released 50 ms after the last
  interrupt. "label" names the device (Nokia: "Internal keypad"),
  "autorepeat" as usual.

N800 DT, after Nokia's board-n800.c: McSPI1 CS0 at 6 MHz, DAV gpio103,
KBIRQ gpio109, reset gpio118, the LS041Y3 panel's touchscreen values
(N800s with the LPH8923 panel had 180 ohm and 100 us settling), and the
keymap: Up, Home (F5), Left, Enter, Right, Cycle (Esc), Down, Menu (F4),
Zoom- (F8), Full screen (F6), Zoom+ (F7).

Not ported: Nokia's sysfs files on the SPI device (pen_down,
disable_ts, disable_kp) and the IRQs as wakeup sources.

Tested in QEMU's n800 machine only (its TSC2301 model): touch and
release, keys (Up, Enter, Zoom+, Down), close and inhibit stopping the
scans, module reload. Not on hardware.

